From 4143c62afe554c7ff54de990bd3fdbad4467fd85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:21:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 00/11] rdna-boosts: block 00: foundation - band-uniformity,
 Meta-wrapper and allocator fixes

Groundwork block (multiple base-level concerns, by design):
- FA KV-split width invariance (launch_fattn, n_q <= 8)
- shared-NextN MTP heads keep their own KV (is_mem_shared gate)
- CPU llamafile_sgemm routes n <= 8 to vec_dot (decode/verify band unity)
- single-device -sm tensor skips the Meta wrapper
- meta-buffer compute-container headroom 16 -> 128 (recurrent snapshot views)
- multi-ubatch logits readback ordering (async D2H race)
- ggml-alloc: release view sources whose views are never consumed (W4)

Sources: old 00, 05, 07, 09a(compute headroom), 06(readback), 15(W4).
